 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool input against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before invoking the executor. Invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field paths and constraints so the model can correct the call; the executor is never invoked on a schema-rejected call. Schema compilation for static tools happens once at `register` time, so an invalid schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation. **Migration note:** an executor that previously hand-validated its own input now only receives input the declared schema already accepts; any code that relied on seeing malformed input to produce a custom error message should be updated, as it will no longer be called with such input.
+
